  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Given $\\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{u}+\\frac{1}{v}$, find the value of $f$ when:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$u=2$ and $v=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f=1\\frac{1}{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{2}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{align*}$$\nTaking reciprocals of both sides gives $f=\\frac{4}{3}=1\\frac{1}{3}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$u=6$ and $v=9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f=3\\frac{3}{5}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{9}\\\\\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{3}{18}+\\frac{2}{18}\\\\\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{5}{18}\\end{align*}$$\nTaking reciprocals of both sides gives $f=\\frac{18}{5}=3\\frac{3}{5}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$u=12$ and $v=11$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f=5\\frac{17}{23}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{1}{11}\\\\\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{11}{132}+\\frac{12}{132}\\\\\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{23}{132}\\end{align*}$$\nTaking reciprocals of both sides gives $f=\\frac{132}{23}=5\\frac{17}{23}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$u=2$ and $v=15$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f=1\\frac{13}{17}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{15}\\\\\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{15}{30}+\\frac{2}{30}\\\\\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{17}{30}\\end{align*}$$\nTaking reciprocals of both sides gives $f=\\frac{30}{17}=1\\frac{13}{17}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
